            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "<p>The study describes rapport management that takes place during physical face-to-face group work interactions and examines the complex negotiation of social categories during intercultural group work interactions.  This ethnographically informed qualitative study involved participants who were first-year undergraduates. The findings confirm that rapport orientation is a key influence in strategy choice driven by the constructed social categories of the participants.</p>"
                }
              }
            ]
